    "content": "<p>Pilots show speed gains and new error modes. Approve tools, require human sign-off, and keep sources controllable.</p>\n<h2>What teams are dealing with now</h2>\n<p>Right now, procurement work centres on <strong>AI governance</strong>. It shows up in live clarifications, evaluation meetings and supplier messages — not in abstract strategy decks.</p>\n<h2>How human review shows up in the process</h2>\n<p>Buyers who treat <strong>human review</strong> as a daily operating need move faster with fewer disputes. Spreadsheets and private inboxes recreate uneven information and weak trails.</p>\n<h2>Why templates belongs in the system</h2>\n<p>Platforms that support <strong>templates</strong> reduce rework: searchable suppliers, public Q&amp;A, guided workflows and logged decisions. Missing capability turns into overtime and failed deliveries.</p>\n<h2>What to do on the next tender</h2>\n<p>Apply the lesson immediately: tighten questions, keep answers public, and keep documents in one place before the next publication deadline.</p>",
